cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pefftacular in your research, please cite the software using these metadata."
type: software
title: "pefftacular: Reading and writing PSI Extended FASTA files in Python"
abstract: >-
  pefftacular is a pure-Python library for reading and writing PSI Extended
  FASTA Format (PEFF) files, a FASTA extension for proteomics annotations. It
  provides an eager read_peff function and a lazy PeffReader for processing
  files without loading every sequence into memory. The parser represents file
  headers, database headers, sequences, and annotations as frozen typed data
  classes. Supported entry annotations include simple and complex variants,
  UniMod and PSI-MOD modifications, processed regions, proteoforms, disulfide
  bonds, and header-defined custom values. The writer serializes these models
  to canonical PEFF text and preserves the escaping rules used in description
  lines. Parsing follows the PEFF 1.0 specification. Structural failures raise
  errors with line, context, and repair hints, while recoverable specification
  violations produce warnings and retain the parsed data. The package targets
  proteomics tools that need programmatic PEFF validation, conversion,
  inspection, or generation. It requires Python 3.12 or later and has no
  runtime dependencies.
authors:
